#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""dev-team: work through a queue of tasks, one fresh Claude session per task.

Each task runs as its own headless ``claude -p`` in the project root, so every
one starts with an empty context and reads CLAUDE.md like any new session does.
Nothing carries over between tasks except what is on disk: the code, git, and
this run's progress file (each finished task's final report), which later
sessions are pointed at in case an earlier task matters to them.

    Scripts/dev/dev-team                           # the queue in Scripts/dev/tasks.md
    Scripts/dev/dev-team -t other.md               # a different task file
    Scripts/dev/dev-team "Add X" "Then fix Y"      # tasks as arguments
    Scripts/dev/dev-team --no-commit               # leave changes uncommitted
    Scripts/dev/dev-team --dry-run                 # show what would run

A task file is a Markdown list. Every top-level item is one task; indented or
following lines up to the next item belong to it, so a task can run to several
paragraphs. Headings and text before the first item are ignored. A line
``effort: <level>`` or ``model: <name>`` under an item sets that task's
session effort or model, overriding --effort / --model. A task with neither
an effort: hint nor --effort is sized first (devteam/triage.py: one Haiku call
for the queue), which runs the small, obvious ones at low effort:

    # Friday queue
    - [ ] Raise the inventory size to 12.
          effort: low
    - [ ] Add a campfire that raises Temperature within 5 m.
          It should burn for 3 minutes, then go out.
    - [x] Already done -- skipped.

A task that finishes is ticked (``- [x]``) in the file as soon as it does, so
re-running the same file resumes where the last run stopped. A failed task
stops the run (later tasks may depend on it) unless --keep-going is given.

The file is read again after each task, so it can be edited while a run is
going: an item added to it is run in this run, in the file's order (and sized
by triage like the rest), and a waiting item ticked or deleted there is not
run. The run ends when the file has no unticked item it has not tried.

**Editors.** Before each task, every editor of this project is closed: asked
through its inbox to save its dirty packages and quit, and terminated only if
it does not. If an editor cannot be closed, the run stops rather than work
beside it. A session gets a warm editor of its own instead (UEPY_SERVE, see
uepylib/server.py): its first uepy.py call boots a headless editor serving
Saved/uepy/devteam, later calls reuse it, and nothing it does reaches an
editor the user reopens meanwhile. dev-team stops it before each sweep, before
asking for a Fab asset, and at the end of the run.

**The gate.** Before each task dev-team runs every verifier suite once, cold,
and puts the numbers in the prompt; after the session it runs them again. A
suite that newly fails -- or fails more checks than before -- sends the
session back (``--resume``) with the failures, up to --fix-attempts times,
then fails the task. --no-gate skips both sweeps.

Sessions run unattended, so they cannot ask questions. The default permission
mode is ``auto`` (a classifier approves or blocks each action); pass
``--permission-mode bypassPermissions`` to allow everything, or a stricter mode
to allow less. Any action that would prompt is denied, not waited on. No MCP
servers are loaded (--strict-mcp-config): no task uses them, and their tools
would be re-read on every turn.

**Fast mode.** A task runs in fast mode (the same Opus, faster output) while
the five-hour session limit is under half used, going by the last reading a
session streamed (devteam/fast.py). --fast on / --fast off override the rule.
Fast mode is billed to usage credits, not to the plan; where it cannot run,
the session runs at standard speed and its ``session`` line says why.

**Fab assets need you.** Sessions cannot sign in to Fab, so an asset a task
needs is asked of you at this terminal: a task's ``fab:`` hints before its
session starts, and a session whose report opens with FAB-REQUIRED after it
ends. You add the asset (Fab plugin in the editor, or the launcher), give the
/Game folder it landed in, and dev-team records it in fab_library.json and
resumes the session. 's' fails the task, 'q' stops the run; with no terminal
(stdin not a tty) the task is failed with the list rather than waited on.
See devteam/fab.py.

Each task's commit message has an "Issues encountered:" section, written by
the session. After the session ends, dev-team adds ``Time:`` and ``Tokens:``
trailers to the task's last commit (a gate fix included), amending only the
message, and never a commit that is already on a remote branch.

Logs go to Saved/DevTeam/<timestamp>/: the raw stream-json transcript of every
task, each task's sweep output, and progress.md with each task's report and
gate table. ``claude --resume <session id>`` opens any task to inspect it.

The pieces live in Scripts/dev/devteam (see its __init__ for the map).
"""

import argparse
import datetime
import os
import sys
import time

HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
sys.path.insert(0, HERE)
sys.path.insert(1, os.path.dirname(HERE))        # Scripts/: asset_pipeline

from devteam import fab, fast, gate                                       # noqa: E402
from devteam.accounting import (                                    # noqa: E402
    describe_time, describe_tokens, git, git_head, merge_results, tag_commit,
    token_usage,
)
from devteam.session import (                                       # noqa: E402
    build_cmd, build_fix_prompt, build_prompt, run_session, session_env,
)
from devteam.tasks import Task, parse_tasks, requeue, tick          # noqa: E402
from devteam.triage import triage                                   # noqa: E402
from uepylib import editors, server                                 # noqa: E402

ROOT = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(HERE, "..", ".."))
LOG_ROOT = os.path.join(ROOT, "Saved", "DevTeam")
DEFAULT_TASKS = os.path.join(ROOT, "Scripts", "dev", "tasks.md")
SERVE_DIR = os.path.join(ROOT, "Saved", "uepy", "devteam")


def parse_args():
    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        prog="dev-team", description=__doc__.split("\n\n")[0],
        formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter,
        epilog="\n\n".join(__doc__.split("\n\n")[1:]))
    p.add_argument("tasks", nargs="*",
                   help="task texts, or '-' to read a task list from stdin "
                        "(instead of the task file)")
    p.add_argument("-t", "--tasks-file", metavar="FILE",
                   help=f"the task file (default: {os.path.relpath(DEFAULT_TASKS, ROOT)})")
    p.add_argument("--no-commit", dest="commit", action="store_false",
                   help="leave each task's work uncommitted")
    p.add_argument("--keep-going", action="store_true",
                   help="continue after a failed task instead of stopping")
    p.add_argument("--permission-mode", default="auto",
                   help="auto (default), acceptEdits, bypassPermissions, ...")
    p.add_argument("--model", help="model for every task (default: claude's own)")
    p.add_argument("--effort", help="effort level for every task (skips triage)")
    p.add_argument("--no-triage", dest="triage", action="store_false",
                   help="don't size the queue first (devteam/triage.py): every "
                        "task without an effort: hint runs at the default effort")
    p.add_argument("--fast", choices=fast.MODES, default="auto",
                   help="fast mode: auto (default: while the session limit is under "
                        f"{fast.THRESHOLD:.0%}% used), on, or off")
    p.add_argument("--budget", type=float, metavar="USD", help="per-task spending cap")
    p.add_argument("--no-gate", dest="gate", action="store_false",
                   help="skip the verifier sweeps before and after each task")
    p.add_argument("--fix-attempts", type=int, default=1, metavar="N",
                   help="times a session is sent back to fix a gate regression (default 1)")
    p.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true",
                   help="list the tasks that would run, then exit")
    return p.parse_args()


def load_tasks(args):
    if args.tasks and args.tasks_file:
        sys.exit("dev-team: give either task texts or -t FILE, not both")
    if args.tasks == ["-"]:
        return None, parse_tasks(sys.stdin.read())
    if args.tasks:
        return None, [Task(t.strip()) for t in args.tasks if t.strip()]
    task_file = os.path.abspath(args.tasks_file or DEFAULT_TASKS)
    if not os.path.isfile(task_file):
        sys.exit(f"dev-team: no task file at {task_file}")
    with open(task_file) as f:
        return task_file, parse_tasks(f.read())


def size(tasks, args):
    """Triage the tasks that have no effort yet. Returns what the call cost."""
    if not (args.triage and not args.effort):
        return 0.0
    unsized = [t for t in tasks if not t.effort]
    cost, error = triage(unsized, ROOT)
    lowered = sum(1 for t in unsized if t.triage)
    print(f"  triage: {error}" if error else
          f"  triage: {lowered} of {len(unsized)} task(s) at low effort, "
          f"the rest at the default (${cost:.2f})")
    return cost


def describe(n, task):
    hints = ", ".join(f"{k} {v}" for k, v in (("effort", task.effort), ("model", task.model))
                      if v)
    if task.triage:
        hints += f" -- triage: {task.triage}"
    return f"  {n}. {task.title}" + (f"  [{hints}]" if hints else "")


def reread(task_file, pending, attempted, args, n):
    """The queue after a task: the task file as it is now (tasks.requeue).

    Returns (queue, triage cost). A file that cannot be read leaves the queue
    as it was."""
    try:
        with open(task_file) as f:
            fresh = parse_tasks(f.read())
    except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError) as exc:
        print(f"dev-team: could not read {task_file} again ({exc}) "
              "-- keeping the queue as it was")
        return pending, 0.0
    queue, added, dropped = requeue(pending, attempted, fresh)
    for task in dropped:
        print(f"dev-team: no longer in {os.path.basename(task_file)}, "
              f"so not run: {task.title}")
    if not added:
        return queue, 0.0
    print(f"dev-team: {len(added)} new task(s) in {os.path.basename(task_file)}")
    cost = size(added, args)
    for i, task in enumerate(queue, n + 1):
        if task in added:
            print(describe(i, task))
    return queue, cost


def close_editors():
    """True when no editor of the project is left running, the session's warm
    one included (asked to stop first; close_editors would only signal it)."""
    if server.stop(SERVE_DIR):
        print("    stopped the session's warm editor")
    _closed, left = editors.close_editors()
    for proc in left:
        print(f"    could not close {proc.binary} {proc.pid}")
    return not left


def tree_state():
    """What a sweep's result depends on: HEAD plus the uncommitted changes."""
    return (git(ROOT, "rev-parse", "HEAD").stdout.strip(),
            git(ROOT, "status", "--porcelain").stdout)


def sweep(label, log_path):
    started = time.time()
    rows = gate.run_sweep(ROOT, log_path)
    if rows is None:
        print(f"    gate: {label} sweep failed to run ({time.time() - started:.0f}s)")
    else:
        bad = [l for l, r in rows.items() if not r.get("ok")]
        print(f"    gate: {label} {len(rows)} suites, "
              + (f"failing: {', '.join(bad)}" if bad else "all passing")
              + f" ({time.time() - started:.0f}s)")
    return rows


def run_one(task, n, total, args, run_dir, progress, cache, meter):
    """One task, gate included.

    Returns (ok, reports, result, gate_table, final sweep or None)."""
    log_path = os.path.join(run_dir, f"task-{n:02d}.jsonl")
    sweep_log = os.path.join(run_dir, f"task-{n:02d}-sweeps.txt")
    env = session_env(os.environ, SERVE_DIR)
    ask = dict(interactive=args.interactive)
    blocked = fab.preflight(task.fab, close_editors, **ask)
    if blocked:
        return False, [blocked], {}, None, None
    baseline = None
    if args.gate:
        state = tree_state()
        baseline = cache.get(state) or sweep("baseline", sweep_log)
    prompt = build_prompt(task, n, total, progress,
                          gate.table(baseline) if baseline else None, args.commit)
    # Decided once: the task's follow-ups keep the speed its session began at.
    task.fast, why = meter.decide(time.time())
    print(f"    fast mode {'on' if task.fast else 'off'} -- {why}")
    common = dict(model=task.model or args.model, effort=task.effort or args.effort,
                  budget=args.budget, fast=task.fast)
    ok, report, result = run_session(
        build_cmd(prompt, args.permission_mode, name=f"dev-team {n}/{total}: {task.title}",
                  **common), ROOT, log_path, env, meter.see)

    def resume(follow_prompt):
        return run_session(build_cmd(follow_prompt, args.permission_mode,
                                     resume=result["session_id"], **common),
                           ROOT, log_path, env, meter.see)

    ok, reports, result = fab.follow_up(ok, report, result, resume, close_editors, **ask)
    gate_table = None
    if not (ok and args.gate):
        return ok, reports, result, gate_table, None
    close_editors()
    after = sweep("after", sweep_log)
    problems = gate.regressions(baseline, after)
    attempts = 0
    while problems and attempts < args.fix_attempts and result.get("session_id"):
        attempts += 1
        print(f"    gate: {len(problems)} regression(s); sending the session back "
              f"({attempts}/{args.fix_attempts})")
        for p in problems:
            print(f"      - {p[:200]}")
        fix = build_fix_prompt(problems, gate.table(baseline, after), args.commit)
        # Triage guessed low and the gate disagrees: fix at the default effort.
        fix_opts = dict(common, effort=args.effort) if task.triage else common
        ok, report, fixed = run_session(
            build_cmd(fix, args.permission_mode, resume=result["session_id"], **fix_opts),
            ROOT, log_path, env, meter.see)
        result = merge_results(result, fixed)
        reports.append(report)
        if not ok:
            break
        after = sweep("after fix", sweep_log)
        problems = gate.regressions(baseline, after)
    gate_table = gate.table(baseline, after)
    if problems:
        ok = False
        reports.append("FAILED: the verifier gate still regresses:\n"
                       + "\n".join(f"- {p}" for p in problems))
    return ok, reports, result, gate_table, after


def main():
    args = parse_args()
    task_file, tasks = load_tasks(args)
    # Fab assets are asked for at the terminal; '-' has used stdin up.
    args.interactive = sys.stdin.isatty() and args.tasks != ["-"]
    todo = [t for t in tasks if not t.done]
    if not todo:
        sys.exit("dev-team: nothing to do (no unticked tasks)")
    skipped = len(tasks) - len(todo)
    print(f"dev-team: {len(todo)} task(s)" + (f", {skipped} already done" if skipped else ""))
    triage_cost = size(todo, args)
    for i, t in enumerate(todo, 1):
        print(describe(i, t))
    if args.dry_run:
        return

    stamp = datetime.datetime.now().strftime("%Y%m%d-%H%M%S")
    run_dir = os.path.join(LOG_ROOT, stamp)
    os.makedirs(run_dir)
    progress = os.path.join(run_dir, "progress.md")
    with open(progress, "w") as f:
        f.write(f"# dev-team run {stamp}\n")

    outcomes, total_cost, cache = [], triage_cost, {}
    attempted = []      # run already and still unticked: not to be queued again
    meter = fast.Meter(args.fast, fast.last_seen(LOG_ROOT))
    while todo:
        # The total moves when the task file is edited mid-run (reread, below).
        task, n, total = todo[0], len(outcomes) + 1, len(outcomes) + len(todo)
        print(f"\n[{n}/{total}] {task.title}")
        if not close_editors():
            print("dev-team: stopping -- an editor of this project is still running")
            break
        before = git_head(ROOT)
        try:
            ok, reports, result, gate_table, swept = run_one(
                task, n, total, args, run_dir, progress, cache, meter)
        except KeyboardInterrupt:
            print("\ndev-team: interrupted -- this task stays unticked")
            outcomes.append((todo.pop(0), "interrupted"))
            break
        except fab.FabStop as stop:
            print(f"\ndev-team: stopped while waiting for Fab asset {stop} "
                  "-- this task stays unticked")
            outcomes.append((todo.pop(0), "stopped"))
            break
        cost = result.get("total_cost_usd") or 0.0
        total_cost += cost
        status = "done" if ok else "FAILED"
        tokens = describe_tokens(token_usage(result), cost)
        took = describe_time(result.get("duration_ms"))
        after = git_head(ROOT)
        if before and after and after != before:
            after = tag_commit(ROOT, before, after, took, tokens)
        commits = f", commits {before}..{after}" if after and after != before else ""
        print(f"    {status} in {took}, ${cost:.2f}{commits}  (log: {run_dir})")
        print(f"    tokens {tokens}")
        report = "\n\n".join(r for r in reports if r)
        if report:
            print("    " + report.replace("\n", "\n    "))
        with open(progress, "a") as f:
            f.write(f"\n## Task {n}: {status}\n\n{task.text}\n\n"
                    f"Session: {result.get('session_id', '?')}{commits}\n"
                    f"Time: {took}\nTokens: {tokens}\n"
                    f"Effort: {task.effort or args.effort or 'default'}"
                    + (f" (triage: {task.triage})" if task.triage else "")
                    + (", fast mode" if task.fast else "") + "\n\n"
                    + (f"### Verifier gate\n\n{gate_table}\n\n" if gate_table else "")
                    + f"### Report\n\n{report or '(no report)'}\n")
        outcomes.append((task, status))
        todo.pop(0)
        if not (ok and task_file and task.line is not None and tick(task_file, task)):
            attempted.append(task)
        cache.clear()
        if ok and swept:
            # The next task's baseline, as long as nothing changes in between.
            cache[tree_state()] = swept
        if not ok and not args.keep_going:
            print("dev-team: stopping (use --keep-going to continue past failures)")
            break
        if task_file:
            todo, cost = reread(task_file, todo, attempted, args, n)
            total_cost += cost

    if server.stop(SERVE_DIR):
        print("\ndev-team: stopped the last session's warm editor")
    print(f"\ndev-team: finished -- ${total_cost:.2f} total, progress in {progress}")
    for task, status in outcomes:
        print(f"  {status:>11}  {task.title}")
    for task in todo:
        print(f"  {'not run':>11}  {task.title}")
    sys.exit(0 if all(s == "done" for _t, s in outcomes) and not todo else 1)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
